<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samori Ture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samori Ture was a West African Muslim leader who built a large state, often called the Wassoulou Empire, in the late nineteenth century. He resisted French colonial expansion for many years before his capture in 1898. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> profile lists his state-building among the movements that drew intellectual and ideological inspiration from the Sokoto model.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samori-ture.jpg" alt="Samori Ture" width="318" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Almamy_Samory_Tour%C3%A9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
